Value:
Tinder applies automated means in content moderation to support: 

(i) detection and identification of potentially violative content and behavior (including spam and potentially inappropriate language); 

(ii) prevention through in-product warning prompts that encourage users to reconsider or edit certain messages before sending; 

(iii) enforcement by enabling certain account actions to be taken automatically in specific contexts (including spam-related enforcement); and 

(iv) prioritization and routing by surfacing automated flags and signals for moderator review, so human teams can focus on higher-priority cases and make decisions in line with Tinder’s policies and guidelines.

For additional information, please refer to Our Approach to Content Moderation (pp. 9–10); Our Commitment to Safety — Safety features (pp. 6–7); Appendix I.A — Own-initiative content moderation (pp. 12–14).
